  "deepDiveData": {
    "lab-m1": "\n    <h2>Lab 1: Android ADB Shell Deep Extraction</h2>\n    <p>Perform live command-line forensic extraction using Android Debug Bridge (ADB):</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 1. Check connected authorized devices:</span><br>\n      adb devices -l<br><br>\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 2. Extract hardware properties (IMEI, Model, Android Version):</span><br>\n      adb shell getprop ro.product.model<br>\n      adb shell getprop ro.build.version.release<br><br>\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 3. Pull live radio logcat buffer to catch tower handoffs:</span><br>\n      adb logcat -b radio -d &gt; /evidence/radio_logs.txt<br><br>\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 4. Create logical backup of all applications:</span><br>\n      adb backup -apk -shared -all -f /evidence/device_full.ab\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m2": "\n    <h2>Lab 2: WhatsApp SQLite Database Carving</h2>\n    <p>Direct SQL queries to extract incriminating messages and recover deleted freelist records:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 1. Open WhatsApp database in read-only forensic mode:</span><br>\n      sqlite3 -readonly /evidence/msgstore.db<br><br>\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 2. Extract messages ordered by timestamp:</span><br>\n      SELECT datetime(timestamp/1000, 'unixepoch', 'localtime') AS message_time,<br>\n             jid.raw_string AS sender,<br>\n             message.text_data AS text<br>\n      FROM message<br>\n      JOIN jid ON message.chat_row_id = jid._id<br>\n      ORDER BY timestamp DESC LIMIT 10;<br><br>\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 3. Inspect unallocated freelist pages for deleted texts:</span><br>\n      PRAGMA freelist_count;\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m3": "\n    <h2>Lab 3: iOS iTunes Backup Manifest.db Decoding</h2>\n    <p>Convert Apple's 40-character SHA-1 file hashes back to human-readable filenames:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 1. Open Manifest.db database:</span><br>\n      sqlite3 Manifest.db<br><br>\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 2. Search for SMS and call history databases:</span><br>\n      SELECT fileID, domain, relativePath FROM Files<br>\n      WHERE relativePath LIKE '%sms.db%' OR relativePath LIKE '%CallHistory.storedata%';<br><br>\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># 3. Copy the hashed file to its true identity:</span><br>\n      cp 3d0d7e5fb2ce288813306e4d4636395e047a3d28 /evidence/sms.db\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m4": "\n    <h2>Lab 4: Telecom CDR Mapping in Python & Folium</h2>\n    <p>Automate plotting of cell tower locations across time windows using Python:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># Python script to generate interactive HTML timeline:</span><br>\n      import pandas as pd<br>\n      import folium<br><br>\n      df = pd.read_excel('telecom_cdr.xlsx')<br>\n      crime_calls = df[df['Duration_Sec'] &gt; 0]<br><br>\n      m = folium.Map(location=[28.6139, 77.2090], zoom_start=11)<br>\n      for _, row in crime_calls.iterrows():<br>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;folium.Marker([row['Lat'], row['Long']],<br>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;popup=f\"Time: {row['Time']} | Tower: {row['Cell_ID']}\").add_to(m)<br>\n      m.save('crime_timeline.html')\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m5": "\n    <h2>Lab 5: Pager POCSAG Signal Interception with RTL-SDR</h2>\n    <p>Capture and decode unencrypted over-the-air radio pager broadcasts:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># Run RTL-SDR receiver piped directly into multimon-ng:</span><br>\n      rtl_fm -f 148.825M -s 22050 - | multimon-ng -t raw -a POCSAG512 -a POCSAG1200 -f alpha -\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m6": "\n    <h2>Lab 6: Smartwatch Health Correlation Forensics</h2>\n    <p>Correlate sudden biometric heart rate surges with crime timestamps:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># Query Apple Health SQLite database for biometric spikes:</span><br>\n      sqlite3 healthdb.sqlite<br>\n      SELECT datetime(start_date, 'unixepoch', 'localtime'), bpm<br>\n      FROM heart_rate_samples<br>\n      WHERE bpm &gt; 130 AND date BETWEEN '2026-10-14 01:00:00' AND '2026-10-14 03:00:00';\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m7": "\n    <h2>Lab 7: Drone Flight Log Decryption (DatCon)</h2>\n    <p>Carve Homepoint GPS coordinates from crashed narcotics drones:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># Convert DJI .DAT binary flight record into CSV and KML:</span><br>\n      python3 DatCon.py -f FLY024.DAT -o /evidence/dji_out/<br>\n      grep -i \"HomePoint\" /evidence/dji_out/summary.txt\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m8": "\n    <h2>Lab 8: Cell Tower Triangulation Calculation</h2>\n    <p>Calculate distance from Timing Advance and intersect three tower circles:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># Distance formula from Timing Advance:</span><br>\n      Distance_Min = TA * 550 meters<br>\n      Distance_Max = (TA + 1) * 550 meters<br>\n      <span style=\"color:#34d399;\">TA = 3 &rarr; Suspect distance between 1,650m and 2,200m from antenna.</span>\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m9": "\n    <h2>Lab 9: Multi-Scene Tower Dump Cross-Matching</h2>\n    <p>Identify the common suspect phone number present across two robbery scenes:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># Python set intersection to find matching numbers:</span><br>\n      scene1_numbers = set(pd.read_csv('tower_dump_scene1.csv')['Phone_Number'])<br>\n      scene2_numbers = set(pd.read_csv('tower_dump_scene2.csv')['Phone_Number'])<br>\n      suspect_common = scene1_numbers.intersection(scene2_numbers)<br>\n      print(\"Common suspect phone found:\", suspect_common)\n    </div>\n  ",
    "lab-m10": "\n    <h2>Lab 10: Section 63 BSA Electronic Certificate Preparation</h2>\n    <p>Drafting a court-admissible electronic evidence certificate under Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam:</p>\n    <div style=\"background:#0f172a; color:#38bdf8; padding:8px 12px; border-radius:6px; font-family:monospace; font-size:0.75rem; margin-bottom:8px;\">\n      <span style=\"color:#94a3b8;\"># Essential fields for Section 63 BSA Certificate:</span><br>\n      1. Identification of device (Make, Model, IMEI, Serial No.)<br>\n      2. Lawful custody statement under Section 94 / 105 BNSS 2023<br>\n      3. Certification that extraction workstation was operating properly<br>\n      4. SHA-256 Cryptographic Hash: e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb924...<br>\n      5. Signature and designation of the certified forensic examiner\n    </div>\n  "
  },
